### UnoCX AI Service - example requests
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (or JetBrains HTTP client) and click "Send Request".
### Postman/Insomnia users: import docs/openapi.json instead.

@base = http://localhost:8000
@token = dev-token
@ws = ws_unocx

### Health (no token needed)
GET {{base}}/health

### Chat - single JSON reply
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "{{ws}}",
  "conversation_id": "demo-1",
  "user": { "id": "u_1", "name": "Priya Sharma", "email": "priya@example.com" },
  "page": { "path": "/help/returns", "title": "Returns" },
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "How long do refunds take?" } ],
  "settings": { "company_name": "UnoCX", "language": "match_customer" }
}

### Chat - follow-up in the same conversation (send the full history)
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "{{ws}}",
  "conversation_id": "demo-1",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "How long do refunds take?" },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "Prepaid orders are refunded within 5–7 business days after the quality check." },
    { "role": "user", "content": "and for COD orders?" }
  ]
}

### Chat - streaming (server-sent events: meta, delta..., done)
POST {{base}}/v1/chat/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "{{ws}}",
  "conversation_id": "demo-2",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "Do you ship to Dubai?" } ]
}

### Handover example (returns action.type = "form")
POST {{base}}/v1/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "{{ws}}",
  "conversation_id": "demo-3",
  "user": { "name": "Ravi Kumar", "email": "ravi@example.com" },
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "I want to talk to a human" } ]
}

### Feedback (use a run_id from a chat response)
POST {{base}}/v1/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "workspace_id": "{{ws}}", "run_id": "run_REPLACE_ME", "helpful": true }

### Add a FAQ source
POST {{base}}/v1/knowledge/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "{{ws}}", "type": "faq", "title": "Store FAQ",
  "content": "Q: Do you have a loyalty card?\nA: No, we use loyalty points in your online account."
}

### Add a website source (crawls pages under this path)
POST {{base}}/v1/knowledge/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "workspace_id": "{{ws}}", "type": "url", "title": "Help centre", "uri": "https://example.com/help/" }

### Upload a PDF
POST {{base}}/v1/knowledge/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="workspace_id"

{{ws}}
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Size guide
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="size-guide.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../knowledge/size-guide.pdf
--b--

### List sources and their status
GET {{base}}/v1/knowledge/sources?workspace_id={{ws}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Re-sync a source after the content changed
POST {{base}}/v1/knowledge/sources/ks_REPLACE_ME/sync?workspace_id={{ws}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Keyword flows
GET {{base}}/v1/flows?workspace_id={{ws}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Quality metrics from real conversations (last 7 days)
GET {{base}}/v1/insights/quality?workspace_id={{ws}}&days=7
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Content gaps: questions the assistant couldn't answer
GET {{base}}/v1/insights/gaps?workspace_id={{ws}}&days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
